        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hisashi Igawa, Akira Kurosawa, Abe Kōbō\n- Roles: actor, film director, screenwriter\n- Works: The Man Who Turned Into A Stick\n- Topics: Japanese cinema, surrealist theater\n\nFacts:\n- Akira Kurosawa was born on March 23, 1910, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- In 1969, Hisashi Igawa starred in Abe Kōbō's production of The Man Who Turned Into A Stick, which was a surrealist play.\n- Akira Kurosawa died on September 6, 1998.",
